{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":47731,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"081b6ae98a080a7a4493ba2fc6f12081","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The area fill vector path: my `d` variable includes 'M ...' then for the area I appended 'L 295 (chartTop+90)...'. But the path data coordinates are relative to the vector node... Actually vectorPaths data coordinates are in the node's own coordinate space. I set data with chartTop offsets included, then also set area.y=chartTop. That double-offsets! Same for line: data includes chartTop+y, and then line.y=chartTop. That means the line renders at 2*chartTop. Problem!\n\nWait — when you set vectorPaths then set x/y, the node is positioned at x/y, and the path coordinates are internal. The line's path 'M 0 (chartTop+72)...' has internal coords starting at y≈chartTop. Setting line.y=chartTop moves it down further. Also resize(chartW,chartH) scales the vector network — resizing a vector scales its paths. The internal height is chartTop+72≈chartY+96+72≈350ish, resize to 90 scales it down massively. This is buggy.\n\nFix: rebuild vectors with internal coords from 0, and don't resize. Let me check and fix with a follow-up call: recompute vector paths properly.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71448abc-987f-4492-83f4-28c59ff3b18f","uuid":"86659164-de3b-487c-ac52-8c7880dcf5a6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:15:32.278Z","thinking_duration_ms":6220}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":47731,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"081b6ae98a080a7a4493ba2fc6f12081","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reasoning summary: The chart vectors have a coordinate double-offset bug (path data already includes chartTop, then node.y set again + resize distortion). Fix by rewriting paths in local coordinates without resize."}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71448abc-987f-4492-83f4-28c59ff3b18f","uuid":"d1a268b0-7337-471e-b68d-27857e9569a0","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:15:33.813Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":47731,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"081b6ae98a080a7a4493ba2fc6f12081","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_49d6ef21","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('4:2');\nconst S = page.children.find(n=>n.name==='03_Strategy');\nconst C = S.findOne(n=>n.name==='Content');\nconst GAIN={r:0.18,g:0.71,b:0.44};\nconst line=C.findOne(n=>n.name==='Growth Chart');\nconst area=C.findOne(n=>n.name==='Chart Fill');\n// rebuild local coords: width 295, height 90\nconst pts=[[0,72],[59,58],[118,64],[177,36],[236,42],[295,6]];\nconst d='M '+pts.map(p=>p[0]+' '+p[1]).join(' L ');\nline.vectorPaths=[{windingRule:'NONE',data:d}];\nline.x=40; line.y=line.y; // keep current y? recompute: chartTop = cardY+96. Find card:\nconst card=C.findOne(n=>n.name==='Projection Card');\nconst chartTop=card.y+96;\nline.x=40; line.y=chartTop;\narea.vectorPaths=[{windingRule:'NONZERO',data:d+' L 295 90 L 0 90 Z'}];\narea.x=40; area.y=chartTop;\n// month labels y\nconst months=C.findAll(n=>n.name==='Month');\nfor(const m of months){ m.y = chartTop+90+8; }\nreturn 'chart fixed, cardY='+card.y;\n","description":"Fix chart vector coordinates on 03_Strategy","fileKey":"6ywbeCjGQ9xjP7DRG8vt97"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71448abc-987f-4492-83f4-28c59ff3b18f","uuid":"250c9f83-f437-4823-92fa-44e56801fe1f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T07:15:42.373Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_0_49d6ef21","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
